      "repair_reason": "- [P1] Manual review is needed because the external protected Gateway/security PR lacks real behavior proof and requires owner acceptance of the admin bridge contract.; Cleared: No dependency, workflow, lockfile, package, secret-handling, or concrete source-level security regression was found; the remaining security-boundary items are proof and owner acceptance. (sha=997cdd0bd135d13905b7dbfb750b8a4c9ce0f08c)",
      "review_summary": "The PR gates Gateway `message.action` requester account/sender/owner provenance to admin-scoped callers, adds optional `effectiveGatewayClientScopes`, switches requester-carrying gateway bridge calls to admin scope, and updates focused tests plus the Swift model.\n\nPR surface: Source +40, Tests +70, Other +7. Total +117 across 8 files.\n\nReproducibility: yes. Source inspection shows current `main` forwards requester identity fields from public `message.action` input for write-scoped clients, while the channel action contract treats requester sender identity as trusted server-injected context.",
      "review_followup": "- [P1] Manual review is needed because the external protected Gateway/security PR lacks real behavior proof and requires owner acceptance of the admin bridge contract.",
